{"intent":{"acceptance_tests":["Returns integer >= 0","If no accounts transfer to 108 within 2 hops, returns 0","Counts each upstream account only once even if multiple paths exist","Excludes account '108' from the count"],"aggregation":["COUNT(DISTINCT source_account.id)"],"assumptions":["Transfers are directed edges from source to destination","Account numbers are unique identifiers","Self-transfers are excluded or irrelevant","Graph contains TRANSFERS_TO relationships with source and destination account nodes"],"entities":["Account"],"expected_shape":"single scalar count value","ordering":[],"predicates":["target_account.account_number = '108'","hop_count <= 2"],"relationships":["Account-[TRANSFERS_TO]->Account"],"uncertainties":["Whether transfers within the 2-hop path must be distinct accounts (no cycles)","Whether to count account '108' itself if it appears in a 2-hop path (should not count target)"]},"question":"How many distinct accounts sit within two transfer hops upstream of account number 108 \u2014 that is, accounts from which money reaches 108 in one or two transfers?"}

